# Code ownership for platform-core.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so order matters: the catch-all comes
# first, then progressively more specific overrides. Pair this with a branch
# ruleset on `main` that REQUIRES code-owner review — and add `github-actions[bot]`
# to that ruleset's bypass allowlist so the digest-promotion job
# (.github/workflows/docker-build.yaml, which direct-pushes to main) is unaffected.
#
# NOTE: replace @org/platform-team and @org/app-team with your real GitHub team
# slugs (or @usernames) before enabling the ruleset.

# Default: the platform team owns everything not matched below.
*                          @org/platform-team

# Application team owns each service's source + co-located k8s manifests.
/services/                 @org/app-team

# …except echo-service, which is the platform's canary self-test.
/services/echo-service/    @org/platform-team

# GitOps registration (ApplicationSets) stays platform-reviewed — it governs what
# is admitted to the cluster (project, namespace, sync policy).
/kubernetes/apps/          @org/platform-team
